# RUSTSEC-2026-0367 / RUSTSEC-2026-0368 / RUSTSEC-2026-0369: zip extraction
# flaws (SUID/SGID bits preserved, symlink targets escaping the destination,
# Unix permissions applied through symlinks). Patched only in zip >= 9.0.0;
# no 7.x/8.x backport exists (RustSec + OSV both list `fixed = 9.0.0`).
#   https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0367.html
#   https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0368.html
#   https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0369.html
# Two copies in Cargo.lock:
#   zip 8.6.0 <- calamine 0.36.1 <- finima-ingest (XLS/XLSX/ODS import)
#   zip 7.2.0 <- candle-core 0.10.2 <- finima-embed / mistralrs (optional
#               `candle` features only; not in the default build)
# Not reachable: all three advisories are in ZipArchive::extract() /
# ZipStreamReader::extract() (writing an archive to the filesystem). calamine
# and candle-core only open the archive and read entries into memory
# (ZipArchive::new + by_name); neither calls extract(), and finima has no
# direct zip dependency.
# Why not fixed now: calamine 0.37 (zip ^9) is a 0.x minor (breaking) bump,
# and candle-core 0.11 still requires zip ^8.6 while mistralrs 0.8.1 (latest)
# pins candle ^0.10.2.
# Exit: drop once calamine >= 0.37 and a candle-core on zip >= 9 are in the
# lockfile (`cargo tree -i zip` shows only 9.x).
RUSTSEC-2026-0367
RUSTSEC-2026-0368
RUSTSEC-2026-0369

